---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../../styles/doc.css';
import HeroEmblem from '../../components/HeroEmblem.astro';
---
<Base analytics={false} title="BIP39 Word Check: Is This Word on the Seed Wordlist? - OpenBitcoin" description="Check a single BIP39 word against the official 2048-word English wordlist in your browser, with autocomplete and near-miss suggestions for typos.">
<main class="wrap doc-wrap">
  <div class="doc-head">
    <div class="doc-kicker"><a href="/tools">Tools</a></div>
    <h1>BIP39 word check</h1>
    <HeroEmblem name="wordlist" />
    <p class="doc-lede">Type one word and see whether it is on the official 2048-word list, with autocomplete for partial words and near misses when it is not. One word at a time: no page here takes a phrase.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="doc-grid">
  <div>
    <div class="wc-card">
      <div class="wc-lab">One word</div>
      <input id="wc-in" class="wc-input" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" autocapitalize="off" autocorrect="off" maxlength="32" placeholder="abandon" aria-label="One BIP39 word to check" disabled>
      <div class="wc-ex" aria-label="Example words">
        <span>Try:</span>
        <button type="button" data-ex="abandon">abandon</button>
        <button type="button" data-ex="satoshi">satoshi</button>
        <button type="button" data-ex="recieve">a misspelling</button>
        <button type="button" data-ex="aba">a fragment</button>
      </div>
      <div class="wc-res" id="wc-res" role="status" aria-live="polite">
        <div class="wc-status wc-mut">Checking the wordlist against its published checksum</div>
        <div class="wc-note">The 2048-word English list is built into this page. Before it answers anything, it verifies its own copy.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="wc-sugwrap" id="wc-sugwrap" hidden>
        <div class="wc-suglab" id="wc-suglab">Suggestions</div>
        <div class="wc-sug" id="wc-sug"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="wc-fine">Never type a seed phrase, a private key, an xprv or a 2FA secret into any website, including this one. This field keeps one word and discards everything after it.</p>

    <div class="wc-warn">
      <div class="wc-wlab">Why there is no phrase box on this page</div>
      <div class="doc-prose">
        <p>A seed phrase typed into a web page is a seed phrase that has left your control. Whoever runs the server can change what the page does between one visit and the next, the browser can cache and autofill the field, an extension can read it, and a single bad deploy turns every visitor's backup into someone else's money. So the rule here is absolute and has no exceptions: <strong>no hosted page on this site accepts a seed phrase, a private key, an xprv or a 2FA secret.</strong> This one takes a word.</p>
        <p>Checking a whole phrase is genuinely useful, because the last word of a BIP39 phrase is a checksum and a damaged backup can often be repaired. That work belongs on a machine with no network. The <a href="/tools/seed-recovery">offline seed toolkit</a> is a single self-contained file you download, disconnect from the internet, and open from your own disk; it does the full phrase, the checksum and missing-word recovery with nothing to send anywhere. Read its instructions before you use it, and never open it while you are online.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-card wc-mt">
      <div class="doc-sec doc-prose">
        <h2>What the list is</h2>
        <p>BIP39 turns random entropy into words a human can write down. The English list holds exactly 2048 entries, which is two to the eleventh, so every word carries eleven bits: twelve words are 128 bits of entropy plus a four-bit checksum, twenty-four words are 256 bits plus eight. The words were picked to be common, unambiguous and clearly different from one another. Bitcoin is not among them. Satoshi is, at position 1,532.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="doc-sec doc-prose">
        <h2>The first four letters</h2>
        <p>No two words on the list share their first four letters, and 103 of the words are only three letters long, so four characters per word is always enough to name a word exactly. That is why steel backup plates stamp four letters per word and stop. If your metal backup recorded four letters, it recorded the phrase. It also means a smudged fifth character is usually harmless, while a wrong first letter is not: check the start of a word before you worry about its ending.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="doc-sec doc-prose">
        <h2>A word being valid proves very little</h2>
        <p>This page answers one narrow question: is this string one of the 2048 words. It cannot tell you the word belongs in your phrase, sits in the right position, or that the phrase as a whole passes its checksum, because it never sees the phrase. A phrase made entirely of valid words can still be wrong, and a phrase that is right for the wrong wallet type is still empty. <a href="/learn/seed-backup">How to back up a seed</a> covers recording them properly, and <a href="/learn/self-custody">self custody</a> covers what a backup is actually protecting.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="doc-sec doc-prose">
        <h2>If a site asks for the whole thing</h2>
        <p>Nothing legitimate needs your twelve or twenty-four words typed into a browser. Not a wallet upgrade, not a support agent, not an airdrop check, not a "validation" page that appeared in a search result or a direct message. The request itself is the fraud, and it is the single most common way people lose bitcoin. <a href="/learn/scams">Common scams</a> lists the patterns; <a href="/wallets">wallets</a> covers software that never asks.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="wc-about doc-prose">
      <p>The list embedded here is the English wordlist from the BIP39 specification, unchanged since 2013, verified in your browser against its published SHA-256 checksum before this page will answer anything. Everything runs locally: no request is made with what you type, and the field is limited to one word by design. To check an address instead, use the <a href="/tools/validate">address validator</a>. Data provenance for the rest of the site is at <a href="/sources">/sources</a>; figures and tools are informational under the <a href="/terms">terms</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <aside class="doc-rail">
    <div class="doc-tile">
      <div class="doc-tlab">The list</div>
      <div class="wc-t"><b>2,048 words</b><i>Two to the eleventh, so 11 bits per word</i></div>
      <div class="wc-t"><b>3 to 8 letters</b><i>103 are three letters; 88 are eight</i></div>
      <div class="wc-t"><b>4 letters identify</b><i>No two words share a four-letter start</i></div>
      <div class="wc-t"><b>English, sorted</b><i>Alphabetical, lowercase, no accents</i></div>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-tile">
      <div class="doc-tlab">Related</div>
      <nav>
        <a href="/tools/seed-recovery">Offline seed toolkit</a>
        <a href="/learn/seed-backup">How to back up a seed</a>
        <a href="/learn/self-custody">Self custody, explained</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </aside>
  </div>
</main>
<style is:global>
  .wc-card{background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:22px 24px}
  .wc-mt{margin-top:14px}
  .wc-lab{font:700 9.5px var(--mono);letter-spacing:.13em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-3);margin-bottom:8px}
  .wc-input{width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;background:rgba(124,140,168,.13);border:1px dashed rgba(255,166,60,.32);
    border-radius:10px;color:var(--price-ink);font:700 16.5px var(--mono);padding:13px 15px;outline:none;letter-spacing:.02em}
  .wc-input:focus{border-style:solid;border-color:rgba(255,166,60,.55)}
  .wc-input::placeholder{color:var(--ph);font-weight:600}
  .wc-input:disabled{opacity:.55;cursor:not-allowed}
  .wc-ex{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:10px}
  .wc-ex span{font:700 9.5px var(--mono);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-3)}
  .wc-ex button{background:transparent;border:1px solid var(--line-2);border-radius:8px;color:var(--ink-2);
    font:700 10.5px var(--mono);letter-spacing:.08em;padding:6px 11px;cursor:pointer}
  .wc-ex button:hover{background:rgba(36,51,78,.55);color:var(--ink)}
  .wc-res{margin-top:16px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px dotted var(--line-2)}
  .wc-status{font:700 15px var(--mono);letter-spacing:.02em}
  .wc-status.wc-ok{color:var(--up)}
  .wc-status.wc-bad{color:var(--down)}
  .wc-status.wc-mut{color:var(--ink-3)}
  .wc-badges{display:flex;gap:7px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:10px}
  .wc-badges span{background:rgba(124,140,168,.13);border:1px dashed rgba(255,166,60,.32);border-radius:8px;
    font:700 10px var(--mono);letter-spacing:.09em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink);padding:5px 10px;white-space:nowrap}
  .wc-note{font:500 13px/1.6 var(--sans);color:var(--ink-2);margin-top:10px}
  .wc-note b{color:var(--ink);font-weight:700}
  .wc-note code{font:700 12.5px var(--mono);background:var(--field);color:var(--acc);border-radius:5px;padding:2px 6px}
  .wc-alert{font:600 12px/1.6 var(--mono);letter-spacing:.03em;color:var(--down);margin-top:9px}
  .wc-sugwrap{margin-top:14px;padding-top:12px;border-top:1px dotted var(--line-2)}
  .wc-suglab{font:700 9.5px var(--mono);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-3);margin-bottom:8px}
  .wc-sug{display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap}
  .wc-sug button{background:var(--panel-2);border:1px solid var(--line-2);border-radius:8px;color:var(--ink-2);
    font:700 12px var(--mono);letter-spacing:.02em;padding:6px 10px;cursor:pointer}
  .wc-sug button:hover{border-color:rgba(255,166,60,.5);color:var(--acc)}
  .wc-sug em{font:600 11px var(--mono);font-style:normal;color:var(--ink-3);align-self:center;padding-left:2px}
  .wc-fine{font:600 11px/1.6 var(--mono);letter-spacing:.04em;color:var(--ink-3);margin:10px 2px 0}
  .wc-warn{margin-top:14px;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid rgba(255,166,60,.4);border-left:3px solid var(--acc);
    border-radius:12px;padding:16px 24px 20px}
  .wc-wlab{font:700 9.5px var(--mono);letter-spacing:.13em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--acc)}
  .wc-about{margin-top:14px}
  .wc-about p{font:500 13.5px/1.65 var(--sans);color:var(--ink-3)}
  .wc-t{padding:7px 0;border-bottom:1px dotted var(--line-2)}
  .wc-t:last-child{border-bottom:0}
  .wc-t b{display:block;font:700 13px var(--mono);color:var(--acc)}
  .wc-t i{display:block;font:500 11px/1.5 var(--sans);color:var(--ink-3);font-style:normal;margin-top:2px}
  @media(max-width:700px){
    .wc-card{padding:18px 18px 20px}
    .wc-warn{padding:14px 18px 18px}
    .wc-input{font-size:15px}
    .wc-status{font-size:13.5px}
  }
</style>
<script is:inline>
(function(){
  /* ================= BIP39 word check, hosted-safe =================
     SAFETY: single-word lookup only. No fetch, no XHR, no beacon, no storage
